    "title": "12 students hospitalized after odor reported at Beaumont middle school - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt Faye ,\n1 days ago Odom Academy Middle School is shown in this Enterprise archive photo. (Fran Ruchalski/The Enterprise) At least 12 students were taken to a local hospital Tuesday morning after reports of a potential gas odor at Beaumont ISD's Odom Academy Middle School prompted an emergency response.\nA subsequent air quality test from the city's fire department and other emergency crews on site detected no gas or hazardous substances at the school, according to information from Beaumont ISD. However, the district is still working with those emergency crews to figure out what caused the problem.\nAn on-campus police officer initially reported the odor in the school's choir room, Beaumont ISD said. Several students reported symptoms including nausea and vomiting.\nBeaumont Fire Department and EMS crews arrived at the school shortly after 9 a.m. Medical professionals assessed the affected students on site before they were taken to the hospital for their symptoms.\nThe district asked parents not to come on campus as authorities continued their investigation at Odom Academy.\n\"The safety and well-being of our students and staff remains our highest priority,\" a news release from Beaumont ISD said. \"We are grateful for the quick response of our emergency partners and will continue to share updates as more information becomes available.\"\nSign up for Beaumont Enterprise newsletters here\nRead the original article on beaumontenterprise.com\n6",
